DrGong wrote:
>
> I have been playing nethack for years, Poorly.   I know Its been at
> least 5 years.   and I have yet really to get deep into the game.

Very likely the biggest cause is 1 of these 2 reasons:

1) Every time a character dies there is a lesson to be learned.
I don't think you're putting in the time in figuring out why this
particular character died and trying to not do that in future games.

2) If your characters keep dying and adjusting your tactics no
longer works, it is time to step back and examine your strategy
instead.  For example if your characters keep dying in melee
combat and no amount of using better weapons is helping, then
it isn't the tactics you are using to do melee combat it's the
stragegy you are following to get into melee combat in the first
place.  This is perhaps the hardest lesson to learn in the game,
that how you're playing isn't about each move but about each
level.

> sometimes its poor luck,

There are top notch players who can advance half of their
characters.  Therefore it is almost never poor luck.

On the other hand - Do you consider "death by typo" to be
poor luck?  Well over half of my characters die because I type
a command wrong.  I answer yes to a prompt without double
checking if it's the prompt I expected, or I attack the wrong
monster or I run into a cockatrice or whatever.  User errors
are not really luck.

